    "slug": "3d-engineering-mastery-bootcamp-win-more-tenders-with-blender",
    "content": "<p><strong>Course Title:</strong></p><p><strong>3D Engineering Mastery Bootcamp: Win More Tenders with Blender</strong></p><p><strong>Tagline:</strong></p><p>Master professional 3D modeling, animation, and visualization — create tender-winning visuals that help you close bigger contracts.</p><p><strong>Target Audience:</strong></p><p>Mechanical, Civil, Structural, Electrical Engineers &amp; Graduates (balanced mix, no prior 3D experience required). Room left for future advanced specializations (e.g., product design, infrastructure visualization, electrical systems).</p><p><strong>Duration &amp; Pace:</strong></p><p>6 weeks (slower, comfortable pace)</p><p>1 session per week × 1.5–2 hours (flexible evening or weekend timing)</p><p>Total learning time: ~10–12 hours + optional homework</p><p><strong>Price:</strong> ₦50,000 (full course)</p><p><strong>Teaser Discount:</strong> Attendees from the 2-hour free session receive ₦25,000 off using code <strong>ENGTEASER50</strong></p><p><strong>Software:</strong> Blender 4.2+ (free) + free add-ons only: MeasureIt, BlenderKit, Node Wrangler</p><p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Ahbideen Yusuf, 3D Generalist &amp; Founder of Tryotek</p><p><strong>Clear Overall Learning Outcomes:</strong></p><p>By the end of the bootcamp, participants will be able to:</p><ul><li>Create precise, dimensionally accurate 3D engineering models</li><li>Animate mechanical assemblies and structural systems realistically</li><li>Produce high-quality renders and short animations suitable for tenders and client presentations</li><li>Export models seamlessly to AutoCAD, SolidWorks, Revit, and other CAD software</li><li>Build a professional portfolio piece that demonstrates immediate value to employers and clients</li></ul><h3>Course Structure (6 Weeks – Slower Pace)</h3><p><strong>Week 1: Foundations &amp; Precision Modeling</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Build confidence with Blender’s modern interface and create accurate engineering parts.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Modern workspace setup for engineers (units, snapping, MeasureIt)</li><li>Creating a precise involute gear using current best practices (Curve + Solidify + Geometry Nodes basics)</li><li>Adding professional materials via BlenderKit <strong>Activity:</strong> Build and dimension a complete gear with bore and keyway. <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Navigate Blender efficiently, produce dimensionally accurate parts, apply engineering materials. <strong>Why Valuable for Engineers:</strong> Start creating parts that look professional enough for tender drawings immediately.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Assemblies &amp; Mechanical Relationships</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Combine parts into working assemblies.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Parenting, constraints, and rigid body basics</li><li>Building a simple gear train with shaft and bearings</li><li>Using Array and Mirror modifiers cleanly <strong>Activity:</strong> Assemble a functional 3-gear system with correct speed ratios. <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Create mechanical assemblies, control movement relationships. <strong>Why Valuable:</strong> Show moving mechanisms in tenders instead of static drawings.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Animation for Tenders</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Bring models to life with clear, client-friendly animations.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Professional keyframing and timing for mechanical motion</li><li>Adding subtle motion blur and camera animation</li><li>Rendering fast, high-quality animations with EEVEE <strong>Activity:</strong> Animate the gear train from Week 2 with realistic rotation and a short fly-through camera. <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Produce tender-ready animations in minutes. <strong>Why Valuable:</strong> Clients remember animated proposals far better than static PDFs.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Structural &amp; Multi-Discipline Modeling</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Apply skills across engineering fields.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Modeling simple structural elements (beams, trusses) for civil/structural engineers</li><li>Basic electrical enclosure and cable routing visualization</li><li>Combining mechanical + structural elements in one scene <strong>Activity:</strong> Create a small bridge section or machine base with integrated mechanical components. <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Model across disciplines, prepare hybrid visualizations. <strong>Why Valuable:</strong> Makes the course relevant to civil, structural, and electrical participants.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 5: Rendering, Presentation &amp; CAD Export</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Deliver client-ready files and visuals.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Professional lighting and HDRI setups for engineering renders</li><li>Creating annotated presentation views with MeasureIt</li><li>Export workflows: .STEP, .STL, .GLB, and high-res image sequences <strong>Activity:</strong> Render a polished presentation sheet and export the full assembly to CAD format. <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Produce photorealistic images, clean exports, and tender visuals. <strong>Why Valuable:</strong> Directly improves proposal quality and win rate.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 6: Capstone Project + Portfolio Ready</strong></p><p><strong>Objective:</strong> Complete a strong tender-focused project.</p><p><strong>Content:</strong></p><ul><li>Guided capstone: Build, animate, render, and export a complete <strong>Tender-Ready Mechanical-Structural Assembly</strong> (e.g., an animated conveyor system, small crane mechanism, or pump station with structural frame).</li><li>Portfolio optimization and presentation tips. <strong>Activity:</strong> Finalize and present your project (2–3 min share). <strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Deliver a complete professional visualization from concept to export. <strong>Why Valuable:</strong> Participants leave with a portfolio piece they can use in real tenders immediately.</li></ul><p><strong>Bonus Graduation &amp; Networking Session (Integrated into Week 6 or optional extra 1-hour session)</strong></p><ul><li>Comprehensive Q&amp;A</li><li>Career pathways: Next steps in 3D for engineers (product visualization, BIM integration, advanced rendering)</li><li>Digital certificate presentation: “Tryotek 3D Engineering Mastery Certificate”</li><li>Portfolio review offer and group networking</li><li>Testimonial recording for marketing</li></ul><h3>Recommended Final Deliverable (Capstone Project)</h3><p><strong>Tender-Ready Animated Pump Station or Conveyor Assembly</strong></p><p>(Recommended because it combines mechanical motion, structural elements, and electrical components — relevant to all disciplines).</p><p>Participants create a clean 3D model, animate the working mechanism, add professional lighting/annotations, render stills + short animation, and export to CAD. This single project demonstrates full workflow and looks impressive in proposals or interviews.</p>",
