    "content": "<p><strong>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</strong></p><ul><li>From Sketch to Screen: Master 3D Fashion Visualization in Just 2 Hours</li><li>Duration: 2 hours (90 min hands-on + 30 min Q&amp;A)</li><li>You will leave with a beautiful 3D Ankara dress ready for client presentations.</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 2 – Why Fashion Designers Need 3D Now</strong></p><ul><li>Traditional sketches &amp; physical samples take weeks and cost money.</li><li>3D lets you show clients photoreal designs in hours.</li><li>Real impact: 70% faster client approvals, 80% fewer physical samples, instant “wow” factor.</li><li>Key stat: “Designers using 3D close 40% more deals on the first pitch.”</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 3 – Blender Crash Course: From Zero to First Garment (15 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Navigate the 3D Viewport confidently, add and transform basic objects.</p><p><strong>What Designers Will Do:</strong> Quick guided tour of Blender 4.3 interface (Viewport, Outliner, Properties).</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong> Add a cylinder (mannequin torso), scale it, and change color.</p><p><strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> You can now turn any sketch into a 3D body in minutes.</p><p><strong>3D Image Prompt for Slide:</strong> “A sleek modern fashion studio with dramatic spotlighting, a glowing laptop showing Blender’s clean 4.3 interface, a simple white digital mannequin in the center, and vibrant Ankara fabric swatches floating nearby, high-fashion editorial style, teal and gold accents.”</p><p><strong>Slide 4 – Building the Ankara Dress – Hands-On (35 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Model a simple dress using basic shapes + cloth simulation.</p><p><strong>Step-by-step (live demo + everyone follows):</strong></p><ol><li>Start with cylinder → sculpt soft dress shape.</li><li>Add plane for skirt → apply quick Cloth modifier (realistic drape).</li><li>Texture with free Ankara pattern (I provide the texture pack in the shared folder). <strong>Activity:</strong> Build and texture your own dress. <strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> Show them the exact fabric movement on a digital model before sewing a single stitch. <strong>3D Image Prompt:</strong> “Photoreal 3D fashion studio, beautiful female digital mannequin wearing a flowing vibrant Ankara print dress with intricate geometric patterns, dramatic rim lighting, floating gold scissors and measuring tape, high-end editorial photography style, teal and gold color theme.”</li></ol><p><strong>Slide 5 – Animate Your Dress: Make It Come Alive (25 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Create a simple 5-second turntable animation + gentle wind effect.</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong> Keyframe a slow 360° rotation + light cloth flutter. Render in EEVEE Next (instant results).</p><p><strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> Send them a short video that makes the garment look alive — they fall in love instantly.</p><p><strong>3D Image Prompt:</strong> “Dynamic 3D scene of the same Ankara dress on a rotating mannequin, fabric gently flowing in soft wind, studio background with runway lights, cinematic motion blur, teal and gold accents, ultra-realistic Blender render.”</p><p><strong>Slide 6 – Real Client Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</strong></p><ul><li>Patient Education → Client Education: Show dresses in different colors, poses, and lighting.</li><li>Teaser for Full Course: In 4 weeks you’ll create full collections, jackets with zippers, and professional lookbooks. <strong>Call-to-Action:</strong> Download your free “Fashion 3D Starter Kit” (Ankara textures + mannequin) + join the 4-week paid program (next cohort date). Special offer: 20% off for teaser attendees.</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Peer Showcase (10 min)</strong></p><p>Mini-challenge: Change one color or add a simple belt. Everyone shares screen for 30-second “fashion critique”.</p><p><strong>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</strong></p><p>Everyone gets a digital “Completed My First 3D Ankara Dress” certificate + group screenshot for Instagram.</p>",
