    "content": "<p><strong>Program Title:</strong> Tryotek’s 3D Fashion Visualization for Designers</p><p><strong>Target:</strong> 10 absolute beginner fashion designers (online Zoom)</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 4 weeks (3 weeks intensive training + 1 bonus graduation &amp; networking week)</p><p><strong>Total Live Time:</strong> 11 hours</p><p><strong>Software:</strong> Pure Blender 4.3+ (no external tools)</p><p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Ahbideen Yusuf, 3D Generalist &amp; Tryotek Founder</p><h4>Clear Overall Learning Outcomes</h4><p>By the end of 4 weeks, you will:</p><ul><li>Confidently model and texture professional garments (dresses &amp; jackets).</li><li>Create realistic cloth animation and client-ready 360° videos.</li><li>Build complete 3D lookbooks that impress clients and win projects.</li><li>Export high-quality renders and animations for Instagram, WhatsApp, and email pitches.</li></ul><h4>Week-by-Week Structure (with training slides for each session)</h4><p><strong>Week 1: Foundations &amp; First Dress (3 hours)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Master Blender navigation + model and texture a complete dress.</p><ul><li>Session covers: Interface tour, basic modeling, Cloth modifier, material nodes, EEVEE lighting.</li><li>Project: Photoreal Ankara dress on mannequin.</li><li>Homework: Create 2 color variations. <strong>3D Image Prompt for promo slide:</strong> Same as teaser Slide 4.</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Jackets, Details &amp; Realism (3 hours)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Add complex details (collars, sleeves, zippers, buttons) using curves and modifiers.</p><ul><li>Project: Tailored jacket with realistic leather/denim textures + Ankara lining.</li><li>Focus: Procedural details (no GeoNodes yet — saved for later courses).</li><li>Why It Impresses Clients: Show exact fit and stitching before production. <strong>3D Image Prompt:</strong> “High-fashion studio, digital mannequin wearing a sharp tailored jacket with vibrant Ankara print lining visible at cuffs and collar, dramatic three-point lighting, floating fabric swatches and pins, editorial style, teal and gold.”</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Animation, Runway &amp; Client Videos (3 hours)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Animate garments with wind/cloth physics, create turntable + short runway walk.</p><ul><li>Project: 10-second animated jacket + dress combo on a walking mannequin.</li><li>Render in EEVEE Next (fast) and Cycles (final beauty).</li><li>Deliverable: Client-ready video file. <strong>3D Image Prompt:</strong> “Cinematic runway scene, two digital models walking in elegant Ankara dress and jacket, fabric flowing beautifully, spotlights, motion blur, high-end fashion show atmosphere.”</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Bonus Graduation, Portfolio &amp; Networking (2 hours)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Polish portfolio pieces, practice client pitches, network with peers.</p><ul><li>Part 1 (40 min): FAQ + advanced tips (quick material library, lighting setups).</li><li>Part 2 (40 min): “What’s Next” pathways (Advanced Garment Collection course, 3D Printing Accessories, Virtual Fashion Week).</li><li>Part 3 (40 min): Project showcase (each designer presents 2-min pitch), digital certificate ceremony, group networking + testimonial recording. <strong>3D Image Prompt for Graduation slide:</strong> “Elegant virtual fashion atelier, 10 smiling designers in professional attire holding glowing certificates, large holographic display showing animated Ankara dress and jacket, celebration balloons in teal and gold, sophisticated networking tables.”</li></ul><h3><br></h3>",
