    "content": "<h3>Teaser Course Outline (Live 2-Hour Session)</h3><p><strong>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</strong></p><p>From Prompt to 3D: Master AI + 3D Creation in Just 2 Hours</p><p>You will leave with a beautiful AI-generated 3D product (e.g., a futuristic wireless earbud case or a stylized robot companion) ready for client presentations or portfolio use.</p><p><strong>Slide 2 – Why Creators Need AI + 3D Now</strong></p><p>Traditional 3D modeling takes weeks to learn and months to master.</p><p>AI lets you generate high-quality 3D concepts in seconds and turn them into real editable models.</p><p>Real impact: 10x faster ideation, instant client visuals, stand out in competitive fields like product design, game assets, or concept art.</p><p>Key stat: Creators using AI+3D workflows complete projects up to 70% faster.</p><p><strong>Slide 3 – AI Image Generation Crash Course (15 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Write effective prompts and generate consistent, high-quality reference images.</p><p><strong>What Participants Will Do:</strong></p><ul><li>Learn prompt engineering basics (subject, style, lighting, composition).</li><li>Generate 5–10 strong reference images using free AI tools.</li></ul><p><strong>Activity:</strong> Everyone generates their own “futuristic wireless earbud case” or “cute stylized robot companion” reference sheet.</p><p><strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> You can now show multiple design variations in minutes instead of days.</p><p><strong>Slide 4 – Turning AI Images into 3D Models – Hands-On (35 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Use free tools to convert 2D AI images into usable 3D geometry.</p><p><strong>Step-by-step (live demo + everyone follows):</strong></p><ol><li>Generate reference images with strong angles and details.</li><li>Import images into Blender as reference.</li><li>Use free add-ons (e.g., built-in or Instant Meshes workflow) or manual box modeling guided by the AI image.</li><li>Quick retopology and basic sculpting to make the model clean and editable.</li><li>Apply simple materials and textures from free libraries.</li></ol><p><strong>Activity:</strong> Build your own 3D model based on the AI-generated concept you created earlier.</p><p><strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> Show photoreal or stylized 3D versions of ideas that didn’t exist 30 minutes ago.</p><p><strong>Slide 5 – Lighting, Rendering &amp; Animation (25 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Make your AI-assisted 3D model look professional with quick lighting and a short animation.</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong></p><ul><li>Set up studio lighting in Blender’s EEVEE renderer.</li><li>Create a simple 5-second turntable animation with gentle camera movement.</li><li>Render a high-quality still + short video.</li></ul><p><strong>Why It Impresses Clients:</strong> Deliver polished visuals and mini-videos that make ideas feel real and exciting.</p><p><strong>Slide 6 – Real-World Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</strong></p><p>Use AI+3D for: product design mockups, game assets, architectural concepts, character prototyping, NFT art, or social media content.</p><p><strong>Teaser for Full Course:</strong> In the complete program you’ll master advanced AI workflows, custom character creation, complex scene building, and professional portfolio-ready assets.</p><p><strong>Call-to-Action:</strong> Download your free “AI + 3D Starter Kit” (prompt templates + free texture pack + sample Blender file) + join the upcoming full recorded course. Special offer: 20% off for today’s attendees.</p><p><strong>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Peer Showcase (10 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Mini-challenge:</strong> Modify your model (change color, add one simple detail, or generate a new variation with AI).</p><p>Everyone shares screen for quick 30-second feedback round.</p><p><strong>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</strong></p><p>Everyone receives a digital certificate: “Completed My First AI-Generated 3D Asset” + group screenshot for social media.</p>",
