    "slug": "master-computer-basics-in-just-2-hours",
    "content": "<h3>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</h3><p><strong>From Zero to Confident: Master Computer Basics in Just 2 Hours</strong></p><p>Duration: 2 hours (90 min hands-on + 30 min Q&amp;A)</p><p>You will leave with a clean, organized computer and your first personal digital note/document ready to use.</p><h3>Slide 2 – Why Everyone Needs Computer Fundamentals Now</h3><ul><li>Feeling stuck when someone says “just send me the file” wastes time and opportunities.</li><li>Basic computer skills save hours every week and reduce frustration.</li><li>Real impact: People who master basics finish tasks 3–5× faster, avoid costly mistakes (like deleting important files), and feel more independent.</li><li>Key stat: “Adults who improve basic digital skills report 65% higher confidence in daily life and work.”</li></ul><p>You don’t need to become an expert today — just confident enough to enjoy using your computer.</p><h3>Slide 3 – Computer Crash Course: From Zero to First Click (15 min)</h3><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Understand basic parts of a computer, navigate the desktop confidently, and use the mouse + keyboard without fear.</p><p><strong>What Participants Will Do:</strong></p><ul><li>Guided tour of the desktop, Start menu, taskbar, and settings.</li><li>Learn proper mouse techniques (click, double-click, right-click, scroll).</li><li>Activity: Create a new folder on the desktop, rename it “My First Project”, and move a sample file into it.</li></ul><p><strong>Why It Helps:</strong> You’ll stop feeling lost every time you open the computer and start feeling in control.</p><h3>Slide 4 – Organizing Your Digital Life – Hands-On (35 min)</h3><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Create folders, name files properly, search for lost files, and keep everything tidy.</p><p><strong>Step-by-step (live demo + everyone follows along):</strong></p><ol><li>Open File Explorer and explore the main folders (Documents, Downloads, Pictures).</li><li>Create a simple folder structure: “Work” → “Personal” → “Learning”.</li><li>Learn the golden rules of file naming (use dates and clear names).</li><li>Activity: Organize 5–10 sample files (I’ll provide a small practice folder in the shared drive) into your new structure. Bonus: Change desktop wallpaper and organize icons.</li></ol><p><strong>Why It Helps:</strong> A messy computer = messy mind. You’ll leave with a clean workspace you’re proud of.</p><h3>Slide 5 – Create &amp; Type Your First Digital Document (25 min)</h3><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Type comfortably, format text, save work correctly, and use basic shortcuts.</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong></p><ul><li>Open LibreOffice Writer or Notepad++.</li><li>Type a short “About Me” page (name, one goal, one thing you learned today).</li><li>Apply simple formatting: bold, bullet points, change font size.</li><li>Save it properly with today’s date in the filename.</li><li>Learn 5 essential keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl + S, Ctrl + C, Ctrl + V, Ctrl + Z, Alt + Tab).</li></ul><p><strong>Why It Helps:</strong> You can now create letters, notes, CVs, or lists without help — and send them confidently.</p><h3>Slide 6 – Real-Life Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</h3><p><strong>How you’ll use this immediately:</strong></p><ul><li>Send emails with attachments without panic.</li><li>Shop online safely.</li><li>Help your children/grandchildren with school assignments.</li><li>Keep important documents organized so you never lose them again.</li></ul><p><strong>Teaser for Full Course:</strong> In the 4-week recorded + live program you’ll learn internet safety, basic Excel/Google Sheets for budgeting, photo editing, and even creating simple presentations.</p><p><strong>Call-to-Action:</strong> Download your free “Computer Starter Kit” (practice files + shortcut cheat sheet + folder templates) + join the upcoming 4-week full course. Special offer: 20% off for today’s teaser attendees.</p><h3>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Peer Showcase (10 min)</h3><p><strong>Mini-challenge:</strong> Add one more folder, type one extra paragraph about what you want to achieve with your computer, and change the document’s title color.</p><p>Everyone shares screen for 20–30 seconds: “Show us your organized folder or your About Me page!”</p><h3>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</h3><ul><li>Open floor for questions (common fears, troubleshooting tips).</li><li>Everyone receives a digital certificate: “I Completed My First Computer Basics Teaser – Now I’m Confident!”</li><li>Group screenshot for WhatsApp/Instagram motivation.</li></ul><p><br></p><h3>Tools Needed (All Completely Free)</h3><ul><li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Windows 10/11 (most common) or Linux Mint (free &amp; beginner-friendly alternative)</li><li><strong>Browser:</strong> Mozilla Firefox or Google Chrome</li><li><strong>Text Editor:</strong> Notepad++ (lightweight &amp; free) or LibreOffice Writer</li><li><strong>File Manager:</strong> Built-in Windows Explorer or Dolphin (on Linux)</li><li><strong>Screen Recorder (optional for practice):</strong> OBS Studio (free)</li><li><strong>No paid software required at all</strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿</strong></p>",
