    "content": "<p><strong>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</strong></p><p>From Idea to Clickable Prototype: Master AI-Assisted UI/UX in Just 2 Hours</p><p>Duration: 2 hours (90 min hands-on + 30 min Q&amp;A)</p><p>You will leave with a polished productivity app prototype (login + dashboard) ready for stakeholder presentations.</p><p><strong>Slide 2 – Why Designers Need AI-Assisted UI/UX Now</strong></p><p>Traditional wireframing and prototyping take days with endless revisions.</p><p>AI + Figma now lets you generate and refine screens in minutes.</p><p>Real impact: 70% faster prototyping, 80% fewer revision rounds, instant stakeholder buy-in.</p><p>Key stat: “Teams using AI-assisted design close 40% more projects on the first review.”</p><p><strong>Slide 3 – Tool Crash Course: From Zero to First Screen (15 min)</strong></p><p>Learning Outcomes: Confidently use Google Stitch + Figma to turn a prompt into a professional UI element.</p><p>What Participants Will Do: Quick guided tour of Google Stitch (prompt bar, AI canvas, export options) and Figma (import, layers, properties panel).</p><p>Activity: In Google Stitch, type a prompt (“minimalist dark-mode productivity app login screen, clean cards, modern sans-serif”) → generate → copy/paste directly into Figma.</p><p>Why It Impresses Clients: You can now turn a vague client brief into a visual prototype in real time during the meeting.</p><p><strong>Image Prompt for Slide:</strong> “Modern minimalist design studio with dramatic soft lighting, a glowing laptop displaying Google Stitch’s clean AI canvas with floating UI components, Figma open on a second screen showing the imported login screen, vibrant electric blue and silver accents, high-tech editorial style.”</p><p><strong>Slide 4 – Building the Productivity App UI – Hands-On (35 min)</strong></p><p>Learning Outcomes: Generate base screens with AI, then refine them professionally in Figma.</p><p>Step-by-step (live demo + everyone follows):</p><ul><li>Start in Google Stitch: Generate the main dashboard layout with one strong prompt.</li><li>Paste into Figma and use auto-layout + components to clean up spacing, typography, and colors.</li><li>Use Google Gemini to suggest micro-copy or alternative color schemes, then apply them instantly in Figma.</li></ul><p>Activity: Build and customize your own productivity app dashboard (task list + calendar view).</p><p>Why It Impresses Clients: Show them pixel-perfect screens with realistic interactions before any developer starts coding.</p><p><strong>Image Prompt for Slide:</strong> “Photoreal digital workspace, large monitor displaying a clean productivity app dashboard in Figma with task cards, calendar widget, and analytics section, Google Stitch interface visible in background tab, electric blue and silver color theme, high-end editorial photography style.”</p><p><strong>Slide 5 – Make It Interactive: Add Flows &amp; Prototyping (25 min)</strong></p><p>Learning Outcomes: Connect screens into a clickable prototype using Figma’s built-in tools.</p><p>Activity: In Figma, link screens with interactive hotspots (login → dashboard → task details), add smooth transitions, hover states, and device frames. Use Gemini for quick suggestions on user flow improvements.</p><p>Why It Impresses Clients: Send them a live, clickable Figma prototype link that feels like the real app — they experience the flow and fall in love instantly.</p><p><strong>Image Prompt for Slide:</strong> “Dynamic view of Figma prototype showing the productivity app flowing through login, dashboard, and task screens with visible connection arrows and device frames, subtle motion indicators, modern tech studio background, electric blue and silver accents, clean high-fidelity render.”</p><p><strong>Slide 6 – Real Client Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</strong></p><p>From Designer Speed → Client Delight: Instantly present multiple themes, device previews, and full user journeys in one shareable link.</p><p>Teaser for Full Course: In the 4-week program you’ll master advanced component systems in Figma, complex AI-generated design systems, automated variant creation, developer handoff, and building complete mobile + web apps.</p><p>Call-to-Action: Download your free “AI UI/UX Starter Kit” (ready prompt library + 10 Figma starter files + Stitch export guide) + join the next 4-week paid cohort. Special offer: 20% off for today’s teaser attendees.</p><p><strong>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Peer Showcase (10 min)</strong></p><p>Mini-challenge: Use Gemini to suggest one new feature (e.g., notification center or dark/light toggle), generate it in Stitch, refine in Figma, and add it to your prototype.</p><p>Everyone shares their screen for a quick 30-second “design feedback” round.</p><p><strong>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</strong></p><p>Everyone receives a digital certificate: “Completed My First AI-Assisted UI/UX Prototype in Figma” + group screenshot perfect for LinkedIn or portfolio.</p>",
