    "slug": "build-your-first-private-productivity-assistant",
    "content": "<p><strong>Full 4-Week Course Structure (8-10) </strong></p><p><strong>﻿Course Title:</strong></p><p><strong>Master Free Local AI: Run Ollama + Hugging Face Models and Build Your First Private Productivity Assistant</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Foundations &amp; Setup (2 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Why local/free AI beats cloud tools (privacy, zero cost, offline use, full control)</li><li>Hugging Face navigation: finding safe, high-quality 2026 models (Qwen3.5 series, GLM-4.7/5, DeepSeek V3.2, smaller Llama 4 variants)</li><li>Ollama + LM Studio/Jan.ai installation on Windows/Mac/Linux + easy model pulls</li><li>Hardware basics: what runs smoothly on 8GB vs 16GB+ RAM laptops</li><li>Hands-on: Pull and chat with 3 small-to-medium free models</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Prompt Engineering &amp; Daily Productivity Use (2 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Writing effective prompts for business and personal tasks</li><li>Comparing strengths of different free models (general chat, reasoning, multilingual)</li><li>Simple web UI with Open WebUI or Jan.ai</li><li>Activity: Generate business emails, market research summaries, meeting notes, and weekly plans offline</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Your First Productivity Assistant (2-3 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Set up a clean chat interface (Open WebUI / Jan.ai / AnythingLLM basics)</li><li>Simple messaging integration (e.g., Telegram bot bridge for chat access)</li><li>Basic agent-like tasks: summarize notes, draft replies, create simple outlines</li><li>Hands-on: Build and test your private assistant that you can access via web or messaging</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Real Applications + Polish (2 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Privacy &amp; security best practices</li><li>Exporting/sharing outputs for clients</li><li>Mini projects: AI-powered business report generator, personal productivity bot, client proposal drafter</li><li>Capstone: Deploy your assistant and run a full demo task (e.g., “Research + outline a service proposal”)</li><li>Bonus: Free starter kit (Ollama commands, updated model list, prompt templates, setup guides)</li></ul><p><strong>Outcome:</strong> Students leave with a fully working, 100% free, private productivity AI assistant running on their laptop — plus clear knowledge of when paid tools might offer extra speed or features.</p><p>This version is tighter, more consistent with the teaser, fully free-tool focused, and aligned with your “no fashion” rule. The progression feels natural and motivating.</p>",
