    "content": "<p><strong>Full Course Title:</strong></p><p>Build Agentic AI Assistants: Master Free Local Tools for Autonomous Productivity</p><p><strong>Full 4-Week Course (~10-12 hours total)</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Deeper Local Setup &amp; Model Optimization (2 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Optimizing Ollama/LM Studio/Jan.ai for better speed and memory usage</li><li>Choosing the right free models for agentic work (Qwen3.5 series, GLM-5.1, DeepSeek V3.2 — updated 2026 recommendations)</li><li>Hardware tips for running medium-sized models smoothly</li><li>Hands-on: Test and compare model performance on reasoning tasks</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Agentic Fundamentals with Free Tools (2-3 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>What “agentic” really means (planning, tool use, memory, iteration)</li><li>Setting up AnythingLLM or Open WebUI for agent workflows + intro to simple open-source frameworks like LangGraph basics or CrewAI community edition</li><li>Prompt engineering for agents (structured output, step-by-step reasoning)</li><li>Activity: Build single-agent workflows for business tasks (research + drafting)</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Memory, Tools &amp; Multi-Step Automation (2-3 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Adding persistent memory so the assistant remembers past interactions</li><li>Simple tool integration (file operations, structured outputs, basic external calls via free local methods)</li><li>Debugging and improving agent reliability</li><li>Hands-on: Create agents that handle real productivity flows (e.g., meeting notes → action items → follow-up email draft)</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Practical Business Applications + Polish (2 hours)</strong></p><ul><li>Building reusable agent templates for common tasks (content pipelines, client research, report generation)</li><li>Privacy &amp; security for agentic systems</li><li>Testing and iterating on your agents</li><li>Capstone project: Deploy a complete agentic assistant that automates a full business workflow</li><li>Bonus: Free starter kit with agent configs, workflows, and comparison notes on paid tool advantages (speed/limits)</li></ul><p><strong>Outcome:</strong> Students leave with autonomous agentic AI assistants that complete complex, multi-step productivity tasks using only free local tools.</p>\\",
