    "content": "<p><strong>Title:</strong> Building Complete Games – Mechanics, Enemies &amp; Level Design</p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>Designed for students who have completed the beginner level or already know basic movement and scenes. Take your skills to the next level by creating engaging gameplay loops with enemies, combat, puzzles, and polished level design. You'll build two full short games — a 3D third-person adventure and a 2D roguelike — while mastering camera systems, AI, and game feel that make players want to keep playing.</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 4 weeks (live or recorded)</p><p><strong>Format:</strong> 8 sessions × 2.5 hours each</p><p><strong>What you’ll build:</strong> A 3D Third-Person Adventure + a 2D Roguelike</p><p><strong>Week-by-Week Breakdown</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Advanced Movement &amp; Camera Systems</strong></p><ul><li>Smooth third-person camera, cinemachine (Unity) / sequencer (Unreal)</li><li>State machines for player animations</li><li>Basic AI pathfinding (NavMesh / Behavior Trees)</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Combat &amp; Enemies</strong></p><ul><li>Health systems, damage, attack animations</li><li>Enemy AI (patrol, chase, attack)</li><li>Weapon pickups and inventory basics</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Procedural Level Design &amp; Puzzles</strong></p><ul><li>Tile-based or modular level creation</li><li>Simple puzzles (pressure plates, doors, collectibles)</li><li>Lighting &amp; post-processing for mood</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Audio, UI/UX &amp; Optimization</strong></p><ul><li>Dynamic sound design, background music</li><li>Polished UI with animations</li><li>Performance optimization (LOD, occlusion culling)</li><li>Playtesting &amp; balancing</li></ul><p><strong>Mini Capstone:</strong> A complete short adventure game with 3 levels, enemies, and multiple endings. Publish on itch.io with a trailer.</p>",
