    "content": "<p><strong>Title:</strong> Professional Game Development – Systems, Multiplayer &amp; Publishing</p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>For serious creators ready for industry-level skills. Master advanced systems like multiplayer networking, procedural generation, dynamic UI, and professional polish. Build a complete multiplayer co-op experience and a standout portfolio piece ready for public release. Learn how to optimize, monetize, and market your games so you can confidently publish on major platforms and attract players or clients.</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 4 weeks (live or recorded)</p><p><strong>Format:</strong> 8 sessions × 3 hours each</p><p><strong>What you’ll build:</strong> A Multiplayer Co-op Game + a Polished Portfolio Piece</p><p><strong>Week-by-Week Breakdown</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Advanced Systems &amp; Data Management</strong></p><ul><li>Save/Load systems, inventory with UI</li><li>Dialogue systems (using free plugins like Yarn Spinner or Unreal Dialogue)</li><li>Procedural generation (dungeons, maps)</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Multiplayer Fundamentals</strong></p><ul><li>Networking basics (Unity Netcode / Unreal Replication)</li><li>Real-time multiplayer (2-4 players)</li><li>Lobby system and matchmaking basics</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Polish, Effects &amp; Monetization</strong></p><ul><li>Advanced shaders &amp; VFX (Niagara in Unreal, Shader Graph in Unity)</li><li>Analytics integration (free tiers)</li><li>In-game purchases &amp; ads (using free SDKs)</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Publishing, Marketing &amp; Portfolio</strong></p><ul><li>Building for multiple platforms (PC, Mobile, Console concepts)</li><li>Creating professional trailers and screenshots</li><li>Steam/itch.io page optimization</li><li>Portfolio website + GitHub showcase</li></ul><p><strong>Final Capstone Project:</strong> A fully featured multiplayer mini-game or a complete single-player experience ready for public release. Students present their game in a virtual showcase.</p>",
