    "slug": "from-zero-to-first-playable-game-with-unity-in-2-hours",
    "content": "<h3><strong>2-Hour Live Teaser Course (Unity Only)</strong></h3><p><strong>Course Title</strong></p><p><strong>From Zero to First Playable Game with Unity in 2 Hours</strong></p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>Jump into game development with Unity — no experience needed! In this fast-paced 2-hour session, you’ll build and play your own 3D endless runner game from scratch. Learn the Unity editor, add a running character, obstacles, jumping, and scoring. Walk away with a fun, shareable mini-game and the confidence to continue creating.</p><p><strong>Tools Needed (All Free)</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Hub + Unity 6 Personal Edition</li><li>Computer with 8GB RAM (16GB recommended)</li><li>Free Unity Asset Store assets (provided links + shared folder pack during class)</li></ul><p><strong>Slide-by-Slide Outline (2 Hours)</strong></p><p><strong>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</strong></p><p>From Zero to First Playable Game with Unity in Just 2 Hours</p><p>Duration: 2 hours (90 min hands-on + 30 min Q&amp;A)</p><p>You will leave with your own 3D endless runner game you can play and share immediately.</p><p><strong>Slide 2 – Why Game Development Matters Now</strong></p><p>One person can now create games that reach millions of players.</p><p>Unity powers many successful indie hits.</p><p>Real impact: Build portfolio pieces, create mobile/PC games, or even start your own indie studio.</p><p>Key stat: Unity is used by over 60% of indie developers worldwide.</p><p><strong>Slide 3 – Unity Crash Course: From Zero to First Scene (15 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Navigate the Unity Editor confidently.</p><p>Live demo + activity:</p><ul><li>Install Unity Hub and create a new 3D project</li><li>Understand Scene view, Game view, Inspector, Hierarchy</li><li>Add ground plane, basic lighting, and a simple character capsule</li><li>Move and color objects</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 4 – Building Your Game World – Hands-On (35 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Create a basic endless runner scene.</p><p>Step-by-step (everyone follows):</p><ul><li>Set up repeating ground tiles</li><li>Add a running character (free asset)</li><li>Place and spawn simple obstacles (boxes, logs, etc.)</li><li>Apply fun materials and skybox (jungle, space, or cyberpunk theme)</li></ul><p>Activity: Customize your level theme and place at least 4 obstacles.</p><p><strong>Slide 5 – Make It Playable: Controls, Jump &amp; Score (25 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Add player controls and core mechanics.</p><p>Activity:</p><ul><li>Add WASD / Arrow key movement + Space to jump</li><li>Make obstacles destroy the player on collision</li><li>Add a running score counter</li><li>Playtest in real-time</li></ul><p>Everyone plays their own game live in class.</p><p><strong>Slide 6 – Real Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</strong></p><p>Use this skill to create games for fun, clients, or your portfolio.</p><p><strong>Teaser for Full Course:</strong> In the 4-week Beginner Unity course you’ll build two complete publishable games, learn C# scripting properly, and publish to itch.io.</p><p><strong>Call-to-Action:</strong> Download your free “Unity Game Starter Kit” (character, obstacles, materials) + join the upcoming 4-week Beginner Unity course. Special 20% off for today’s attendees.</p><p><strong>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Showcase (10 min)</strong></p><p>Mini-challenge: Change your game theme or increase jump height.</p><p>Everyone shares their game for 20–30 seconds + fun group feedback.</p><p><strong>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</strong></p><p>Digital certificate: “I Built My First Unity Game in 2 Hours!”</p><p>Group screenshot + final tips.</p>",
