    "content": "<h3><strong>Full 4-Week Beginner Course (Unity Only)</strong> – Detailed Outline</h3><p><strong>Course Title</strong></p><p><strong>From Zero to First Playable Game with Unity in 4 Weeks</strong></p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>No prior experience required. This beginner-friendly course takes you from complete beginner to confidently building and publishing real games using Unity. Through hands-on projects, you’ll master the editor, C# scripting basics, physics, and game feel — ending with two complete games you can proudly share.</p><p><strong>Tools Needed (All Free)</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Hub + Unity 6 Personal Edition</li><li>Visual Studio Community</li><li>Blender (optional for simple edits)</li><li>Audacity + GIMP/Krita</li><li>itch.io + GitHub accounts</li></ul><p><strong>What you’ll build:</strong></p><ul><li>3D Endless Runner (Week 4)</li><li>2D Platformer (Week 4)</li></ul><p><strong>Detailed 4-Week Structure</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Unity Foundations &amp; First Scene</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Editor deep dive (interface, shortcuts, best practices)</li><li>Scenes, GameObjects, Components, Prefabs</li><li>Basic lighting, materials, and skyboxes</li><li>Importing free assets</li><li>Hands-on: Build a beautiful 3D environment in your chosen theme</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Player Movement &amp; Physics</strong></p><ul><li>C# scripting fundamentals</li><li>Character Controller &amp; Input System</li><li>Jumping, running, gravity</li><li>Collision detection</li><li>Hands-on: Fully functional running + jumping character</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Mechanics, Spawning &amp; Scoring</strong></p><ul><li>Object spawning &amp; destruction</li><li>Score system + high score saving</li><li>Particle effects and simple animations</li><li>Sound effects integration</li><li>Hands-on: Add obstacles, coins, and game over conditions</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Polish, UI &amp; Publishing</strong></p><ul><li>Menus (Start, Game Over, Restart)</li><li>UI Canvas and TextMeshPro</li><li>Building the game (Windows + WebGL)</li><li>Publishing to itch.io</li><li>Final project + playtesting</li></ul><p><strong>Capstone:</strong> Publish both games on itch.io and present them in class.</p>",
