    "content": "<h3><strong>Level 2: Intermediate Course</strong></h3><p><strong>Course Title</strong></p><p><strong>Building Engaging Games with Unity – AI, Combat &amp; Polish in 4 Weeks</strong></p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>For students who have completed the Beginner course or already know basic Unity movement and scenes. This level takes your skills further by teaching you how to create addictive gameplay loops, smart enemies, combat systems, and polished experiences. You will build two complete, more ambitious games while mastering camera work, animations, level design, and game feel that keeps players coming back.</p><p><strong>Tools Needed (All Free)</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Hub + Unity 6 Personal Edition</li><li>Visual Studio Community</li><li>Blender (for simple custom models)</li><li>Audacity (audio editing)</li><li>GIMP or Krita (textures)</li><li>itch.io + GitHub accounts</li></ul><p><strong>What you’ll build:</strong></p><ul><li>3D Third-Person Adventure Game</li><li>2D Roguelike Game</li></ul><p><strong>Detailed 4-Week Structure</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Advanced Movement &amp; Camera Systems</strong></p><ul><li>Cinemachine camera setups (third-person follow, dynamic angles)</li><li>Animator Controller &amp; animation blending</li><li>Character state machines</li><li>Input System (advanced actions)</li><li>Hands-on: Smooth third-person character with sprint, crouch, and climbing</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Combat, Enemies &amp; AI</strong></p><ul><li>Health &amp; damage systems</li><li>Basic enemy AI using NavMesh</li><li>Attack animations and hit detection</li><li>Weapon pickup system</li><li>Hands-on: Create patrolling enemies that chase and attack the player</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: Level Design, Puzzles &amp; Progression</strong></p><ul><li>Modular level building with prefabs</li><li>Simple puzzles (keys, pressure plates, doors)</li><li>Collectibles and progression systems</li><li>Lighting, post-processing, and mood creation</li><li>Hands-on: Design multiple connected levels/rooms</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Polish, Audio, UI &amp; Playtesting</strong></p><ul><li>Dynamic sound design and music</li><li>Animated UI with menus and feedback</li><li>Particle systems and screen effects</li><li>Game balancing and playtesting</li><li>Building and publishing updated versions to itch.io</li></ul><p><strong>Capstone:</strong> Complete a short 3D adventure game (with 3–4 levels, enemies, and basic story) + a 2D roguelike prototype. Present both in class with recorded gameplay.</p>",
