    "content": "<h3><strong>Level 3: Advanced Course</strong></h3><p><strong>Course Title</strong></p><p><strong>Professional Unity Development – Multiplayer, Systems &amp; Publishing</strong></p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><p>For developers ready for industry-level skills. This advanced course focuses on complex systems, multiplayer networking, high-end polish, and professional publishing practices. You will create production-ready features and a standout portfolio game that demonstrates you can build games others want to play and pay for.</p><p><strong>Tools Needed (All Free)</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Hub + Unity 6 Personal Edition</li><li>Visual Studio Community</li><li>Blender, Audacity, GIMP/Krita</li><li>itch.io + GitHub accounts</li><li>Free tiers of analytics and ad SDKs (when applicable)</li></ul><p><strong>What you’ll build:</strong></p><ul><li>Multiplayer Co-op Game</li><li>Polished Portfolio-Ready Single-Player Experience</li></ul><p><strong>Detailed 4-Week Structure</strong></p><p><strong>Week 1: Advanced Systems &amp; Data Management</strong></p><ul><li>Save/Load systems with JSON or Scriptable Objects</li><li>Inventory, crafting, and dialogue systems</li><li>Procedural generation basics (levels, items)</li><li>Event systems and architecture best practices</li><li>Hands-on: Robust inventory + dialogue-driven quest system</li></ul><p><strong>Week 2: Multiplayer Fundamentals</strong></p><ul><li>Unity Netcode for GameObjects</li><li>Networking basics (synchronization, authority)</li><li>Lobby system and player joining</li><li>Real-time multiplayer interactions (2–4 players)</li><li>Hands-on: Turn a single-player scene into a co-op experience</li></ul><p><strong>Week 3: High-End Polish &amp; Visual Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Shader Graph and custom visuals</li><li>Advanced particle systems and VFX</li><li>Optimization techniques (LOD, occlusion culling, profiling)</li><li>Performance tuning for different platforms</li><li>Hands-on: Dramatic visual upgrades and effects</li></ul><p><strong>Week 4: Publishing, Marketing &amp; Professional Portfolio</strong></p><ul><li>Building for multiple platforms (PC, Web, Mobile concepts)</li><li>Creating professional trailers, screenshots, and store pages</li><li>Steam/itch.io optimization and SEO</li><li>Analytics, basic monetization, and community building</li><li>Final portfolio website setup</li></ul><p><strong>Capstone:</strong> A fully playable multiplayer co-op mini-game + one polished single-player game suitable for public release. Students will present their games in a virtual showcase with trailers.</p>",
