    "slug": "build-your-first-unreal-engine-game-scene-with-ai-in-just",
    "content": "<p><strong>Course Title:</strong></p><p><strong>Build Your First Unreal Engine Game Scene with AI in Just 2 Hours</strong></p><p><strong>Description:</strong></p><p>Jump into modern game development in a single fun 2-hour live session. Using Unreal Engine 5 (free) and free AI tools, you’ll create a complete mini scene — a stylized sci-fi corridor with interactive elements, AI-generated textures, and a simple playable character. Perfect for aspiring indie devs, hobbyists, and creatives who want to see their ideas come to life instantly. By the end, you’ll have a shareable mini-demo ready for portfolios or social media.</p><p><strong>Tools Needed (All Free):</strong></p><ul><li>Unreal Engine 5 (Epic Games Launcher)</li><li>Blender (optional for quick asset tweaks)</li><li>Free AI tools: Bing Image Creator / Grok Imagine / Leonardo.ai (free tier) for texture generation</li><li>Free Unreal Marketplace assets (Starter Content + basic templates)</li><li>Epic Games account (required for Unreal)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Slide 1 – Title &amp; Welcome</strong></p><p><strong>Build Your First Unreal Engine Game Scene with AI in Just 2 Hours</strong></p><p>Duration: 2 hours (90 min hands-on + 30 min Q&amp;A)</p><p>You will leave with a cool, interactive sci-fi corridor scene you can walk around in.</p><p><strong>Slide 2 – Why Game Development with Unreal + AI Matters Now</strong></p><p>Traditional game prototyping takes months and costs money.</p><p>Unreal Engine 5 + AI lets you create stunning scenes in hours.</p><p>Real impact: 60% faster prototyping, photoreal or stylized visuals with AI textures, and instant “wow” moments for pitches or social posts.</p><p>Key stat: “Indie developers using UE5 + AI tools ship playable prototypes 3x faster.”</p><p><strong>Slide 3 – Unreal Engine Crash Course: From Zero to First Scene (15 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Navigate the Unreal Editor confidently, understand the basics of Levels, Actors, and Blueprints.</p><p><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong> Quick guided tour of Unreal Engine 5.4 interface (Viewport, Content Browser, World Outliner, Details panel).</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong> Create a new Blank project with Starter Content, add and transform basic shapes (Cube, Cylinder).</p><p><strong>Why It Impresses:</strong> You can now turn any game idea into a 3D environment in minutes.</p><p><strong>Slide 4 – Building the Sci-Fi Corridor – Hands-On (35 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Model a basic environment using BSP brushes + AI textures, add lighting.</p><p><strong>Step-by-step (live demo + everyone follows):</strong></p><ul><li>Use BSP brushes to quickly block out a futuristic corridor.</li><li>Generate sci-fi wall/floor textures with free AI tools (prompt provided).</li><li>Import and apply textures + materials.</li><li>Add dynamic lighting and post-processing for cinematic feel. <strong>Activity:</strong> Build and texture your own corridor section. <strong>Why It Impresses Clients/Portfolio:</strong> Show photoreal or stylized environments before writing a single line of code.</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 5 – Make It Interactive &amp; Alive with Blueprints + AI (25 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Learning Outcomes:</strong> Add simple player movement and AI-enhanced elements.</p><p><strong>Activity:</strong></p><ul><li>Add a First Person Character and enable walking.</li><li>Create a simple interactive door with Blueprint (open on overlap).</li><li>Use AI to generate a holographic decal or animated texture and apply it. <strong>Render/Play:</strong> Walk through your scene in real-time. <strong>Why It Impresses:</strong> Share a playable mini-demo that makes viewers say “I want to play more!”</li></ul><p><strong>Slide 6 – Real-World Applications &amp; Next Steps (15 min)</strong></p><p>Turn ideas into interactive prototypes for portfolios, game jams, or client pitches.</p><p><strong>Teaser for Full Course:</strong> In the complete program you’ll build full small games, advanced AI behaviors, multiplayer elements, and polished releases.</p><p><strong>Call-to-Action:</strong> Download your free “Unreal + AI Starter Kit” (project template + texture prompts + asset list) + join the full paid program (next cohort date). Special offer: 20% off for teaser attendees.</p><p><strong>Slide 7 – Hands-On Challenge &amp; Peer Showcase (10 min)</strong></p><p><strong>Mini-challenge:</strong> Add one extra interactive element (glowing button, moving platform, or AI-generated prop).</p><p>Everyone shares screen for quick “dev critique” and applause.</p><p><strong>Slide 8 – Q&amp;A, Certificates &amp; Group Photo</strong></p><p>Everyone receives a digital “I Built My First Unreal Game Scene” certificate + group screenshot for LinkedIn/Discord/Instagram.</p>",
